Subject: bzip2.c: on OpenVMS, a $-prefixed BZIP2 or BZIP is not options

bzip2 reads extra options from the environment variables BZIP2 and BZIP.
The VMS C RTL's getenv() also returns DCL symbols, and the usual way to
run bzip2 is the foreign command bzip2 :== $dev:[dir]BZIP2.EXE: bzip2 took
its own image as a file to compress.  Ignore a value starting with "$" (a
foreign command); a logical name or symbol holding options still works.

--- a/bzip2.c	2026-10-05 10:54:21.568294011 +0100
+++ b/bzip2.c	2026-10-05 10:54:21.558311441 +0100
@@ -1760,6 +1760,11 @@
    Char *envbase, *p;
 
    envbase = getenv(varName);
+#ifdef __VMS
+   /* getenv() also returns DCL symbols, and "bzip2" is the foreign command
+      ($dev:[dir]BZIP2.EXE) that runs bzip2 itself: not options.  */
+   if (envbase != NULL && envbase[0] == '$') envbase = NULL;
+#endif
    if (envbase != NULL) {
       p = envbase;
       i = 0;
